{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/825287-the-triangle-the-jiang-shi","id":825287,"title":"The Triangle & The Jiang shi","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-06T22:55:16-08:00","id":825287,"title":"The Triangle & The Jiang shi","content":"So one of my friends is thinking about running a game using this setting from the 2e core, since we all like it generally and he actually lives there, so he knows all sorts of cool insider knowledge about the area. I was wondering, have any of you guys used this setting? If so, do you have any content created for use with it? Wanna share any interesting stories about it? If you haven't played in it, what do you think just by reading the entry in the Requiem core?<br /> <br /> Related to that, what do you guys think of the Jiangshi? I really dig the flavor and the unique template stuff they get, but I will admit their Discipline spread leaves me kind of cold. Does anyone have any thoughts on these guys or expanded ideas on content for them? What do you think is going on with their inclusion there in the Triangle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T23:31:26-08:00","id":825292,"title":"","content":"I've been prepping to use the Jiang Shi in some upcoming arcs, and can agree that their spread is less than impressive. I haven't typed them up as a full clan, but I do have some notes on my personal adaptation. <hr /><b>Clan: Jiang Shi</b><ul><li><b>Clan Attributes</b>: Strength &amp; Intelligence</li> <li><b>Clan Disciplines</b>: Animalism, <i><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1q3dMgL9v7Vryw-uvWzJ8meJrvvQDjGD6_vjJLPGCjso/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Subvolo </a></i>&amp; Vigor</li> <li><b>Clan Curse</b>: <b>The Gravebound Curse</b></li> </ul><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>\u200b</b><b>\u200b</b>The Jiang Shi are bound to slumber in the soil of their demise. Each morning, at sunrise, so long as the Jiang Shi is within Humanity times ten miles of their burial soil they will 'fade out', teleporting instantly across the intervening distance to sleep in their grave dirt. This may be resisted as any kindred may resist the Daysleep, though should they fail the roll they will be transported. As a bonus, a Jiang Shi may spend a point of Willpower at any point during the night to begin their slumber early and teleport back to the grave, assuming of course that they are within range.<br /> However, if the Jiang Shi is <b>not </b>within Humanity times ten miles of their burial soil, and fails her roll to resist the daysleep, she immediately enter frenzy, motivated with the exclusive goal of returning to the grave. The Jiang Shi will do anything, with the exception of exposing herself to banes, to return to her grave. This frenzy persists, scene to scene until the Jiang Shi comes within Humanity times ten miles of her grave, she is forced into torpor, or the sun sets. Fortunately it is possible, though difficult, for a Jiang Shi to move her gravesite. This requires at least fifty pounds worth of grave dirt be transplanted from her old grave to the new location, where she must spend a willpower dot and sleep one full, uninterrupted day.</div><hr /><br /> Now, for some explanations. I chose Vigor to justify the jumping zombie trope, and Animalism and Subvolo to recreate the sorcerous feel of the Jiang Shi without going so far as to give them sorcery (which is more a Covenant thing). Adapting their grave teleportation power was a little tricky, but I settled on folding it into their bane to give them a somewhat landlocked feel.<br /> <br /> I hope this helps.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>It's worth noting I consider it a tossup between giving them Animalism and Obfuscate. Animalism hit the scary master of natural forces button, while Obfuscate lights on the creepy ghost side and meshes well with subvolo for those interested in playing the poltergeist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 02-07-2016, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T23:46:31-08:00","id":825296,"title":"","content":"I haven't used it in game but I live in the area, too. I think the write-up was pretty apt, but it didn't seem to really get across how backwards parts of it can be. There's a house down the street that flies a confederate flag and has a sign outside that says 'Gay Nuptials' with a noose around it.<br /> <br /> The Jiangshi are pretty cool, but yeah it would have been nice to get their own Discipline. Still, I like what they have. I imagine their high population is due to Jiangshi emigration. I thought it mentioned the increasing Asian population but I don't see it right now. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demographics_of_North_Carolina#Asian_Americans\" target=\"_blank\">There's a high, and growing, Asian American population</a>. I figured some decided to take advantage of the facilities available and started churning out childer until there was a stable population of decent size. I admit it's a fairly simple explanation but sometimes that's all there is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T05:08:48-08:00","id":825360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/825287-the-triangle-the-jiang-shi#post825287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related to that, what do you guys think of the Jiangshi? I really dig the flavor and the unique template stuff they get, but I will admit their Discipline spread leaves me kind of cold. Does anyone have any thoughts on these guys or expanded ideas on content for them? What do you think is going on with their inclusion there in the Triangle?</div> </div> </div> </div> I have used the Jiang Shi, but not in the Triangle. I think they're pretty cool, though none of my players really bit at them, probably because some of the ideas I had were kind of strange:<br /> <br /> The Jiang Shi are vampires-as-ghosts-or-spirits. They move around as ghosts to anchors, they're insubstantial in a way. They don't get any physical disciplines for this reason. I also gave them breath drinking and a unique signature Discipline based on the strix's ability to manipulate fate. Their eyes also ended up as owl-ish, hinting at a stronger strix-connection than other vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T11:09:06-08:00","id":825481,"title":"","content":"I was struck by inspiration to write up the older Jiang Shi as being less-Kindred like using the mechanical framework of a Bloodline. These are probably the oldest Jiang Shi who made their way to the Triangle.<br /> <br /> They're not necessarily made for players to play them, with the idea being that NPCs would be the older Jiang Shi, but there's some stuff in there for players if they choose to use it. Their weird powers are largely inspired by the Jiangshi as they appear in Wicked Dead.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cvP-jVE848m0XIl_leUNITDaMPQ5LTbeKqrvYAykdk4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">True Jiang Shi, the Old Ones</a><br /> <br /> I figured this gave them a bunch of scary, interesting powers and more severe weaknesses to represent that their Blood is less diluted by the Kindred, and make for some cool encounters between players and the Jiang Shi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 02-07-2016, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:05:29-08:00","id":826190,"title":"","content":"So separate from the topic of the Jiang Shi, there's one bit from the Triangle that's sort of interesting to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire the Requiem 2nd Edition, page 255</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A controversial figure, to say the least, the Reverend Rawlins Cartwright is technically merely Mister Cartwright. However, this Serpent\u2019s charismatic nature and unusually polished speech-writing skill has rendered him an authority in the ranks of the Lancea et Sanctum. What this tall, severe man of S\u00e1mi descent preaches is considered heresy by orthodox Sanctified doctrine, and many of the church\u2019s leaders despise the Reverend for this, adding it to their own personal grudges. His long-due reckoning has been postponed because of his popularity, and his hard-line stance proves very popular with troubled young vampires.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to make sure for my own understanding of the Sanctum that I have this right. What would be considered heresy in this case? They mention that his long-due reckoning isn't coming because of his popularity, and that he has a &quot;hard-line stance.&quot; Does anyone have any thoughts on what a Sanctified hardliner would be, especially compared with the Triangle orthodoxy?<br /> <br /> Is he supposed to be sort of like a Solomon Birch figure? If so, what exactly would describe their ideology, and how does it differ from the Sanctified orthodoxy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T21:37:05-08:00","id":826545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/825287-the-triangle-the-jiang-shi?p=826190#post826190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So separate from the topic of the Jiang Shi, there's one bit from the Triangle that's sort of interesting to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I just want to make sure for my own understanding of the Sanctum that I have this right. What would be considered heresy in this case? They mention that his long-due reckoning isn't coming because of his popularity, and that he has a &quot;hard-line stance.&quot; Does anyone have any thoughts on what a Sanctified hardliner would be, especially compared with the Triangle orthodoxy?<br /> <br /> Is he supposed to be sort of like a Solomon Birch figure? If so, what exactly would describe their ideology, and how does it differ from the Sanctified orthodoxy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nobody likes to state the obvious, but here it goes anyway: it's left to the interpretation of the ST. You're supposed to ask yourself these questions when fleshing out the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass","name":"Aiwass","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T22:11:58-08:00","id":826564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiwass</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/825287-the-triangle-the-jiang-shi?p=826545#post826545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody likes to state the obvious, but here it goes anyway: it's left to the interpretation of the ST. You're supposed to ask yourself these questions when fleshing out the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! I'm just asking for what peoples thoughts on a &quot;hard-lining stance&quot; for the Lancea et Sanctum. What would it take for the orthodoxy to find it too extreme? I'm less asking for word of god and more asking for ideas based upon people's knowledge of what might be considered Sanctified orthodoxy. The reason I went to Solomon Birch was because he too is also presented with the idea that he is a radical, and that he is a hard liner on things like not Embracing people, since the Sanctified orthodoxy seems to frown on the Embrace as an unfortunate but inevitable component of the Curse.<br /> <br /> So that's <i>one </i>idea of a Sanctified who is a hard-liner that's a bit too radical for the moderate Sanctified. What might others be? What thoughts do people have on that?<br /> <br /> <br /> For my own thoughts, I find the idea that his hardlining stance appeals to &quot;troubled young vampires&quot; is particularly interesting. Are they perhaps troubled with the whole idea of being Damned? How might that manifest? Does Cartwright advocate that they punish sinners with a righteous zeal, focusing on those outside the church? Maybe a more mainstream Sanctified might dislike that, because it's taking the focus away from<i> testing the faithful </i>if they just focus on punishing supposed sinners.<br /> <br /> That's one idea. Do you have any thoughts on what kind of radical Cartwright might be, or what it takes to be a radical in the eyes of the mainstream Sanctified?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T04:22:27-08:00","id":826697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/825287-the-triangle-the-jiang-shi?p=826564#post826564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure! I'm just asking for what peoples thoughts on a &quot;hard-lining stance&quot; for the Lancea et Sanctum. What would it take for the orthodoxy to find it too extreme? I'm less asking for word of god and more asking for ideas based upon people's knowledge of what might be considered Sanctified orthodoxy.<br /> That's one idea. Do you have any thoughts on what kind of radical Cartwright might be, or what it takes to be a radical in the eyes of the mainstream Sanctified?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that would be considered heretical to the prototypical orthodoxy of the Lance for being too extremist (in its execution) but popular with younger vampires (I am interpreting younger vampires to mean contemporary.) would most likely be one of two things. A doctrinal talking point along the lines that says &quot;all vampires are fulfilling God's role even if they're worshipping other gods or not paying tithes and making regularly scheduled attendance to the church establishment.&quot; It's the vampire equivalent of &quot;everyone goes to Heaven if they're nice&quot; spiel and lets younger adherents off the hook from the requirement of harassing Cruac practitioners and proselytizing to Dragons.<br /> The other may be that he suffers from Robin Hood syndrome, where he and a few others forcibly seize a few herd members or hunting privileges from the wealthiest and feed the younger/poorer and vampires and justifies it as testing the faithful and ensuring they are fulfilling their obligations of charity. The Invictus end up tolerating it because it's considered a sign of noblesse oblige. (If they're targetted then it's a statement from the Church that they're wealthy and makes the prospect of pledging fealty to them look appealing to others.) and the Sanctified orthodoxy didn't care, until its their own rich bishops and deacons who are victimized by this practice, then it gets translated as robbing church coffers. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T05:15:49-08:00","id":827424,"title":"","content":"I would base him off of the woman (you'll know which one I'm talking about) from the documentary Jesus Camp. Said controversial camp trains children to grow up to be born again evangelical neo-con politicians and the like. Remember how in your face American Christianity can be, just as the constant bombardment of advertisement spam. He could be mobilizing neonates and fledglings who like the idea that there is no hierarchy between Kindred under the Lord, justifying extreme acts of violence with the mighty power of rationality and theban miracles making all claims legit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass","name":"Aiwass","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T14:23:47-08:00","id":827789,"title":"","content":"Going back and re-reading Solomon Birch's write-up in <i>Chicago </i>I realized he's a fundamentalist, not a radical, so his way of doing things is merely a stricter interpretation of the Testament of Longinus.<br /> <br /> I had the idea to go back to the Tollison Creed for inspiration, so I'm going to look that over now.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7876_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7876\" data-vbnamecard=\"7876\">Aiwass</a> I suppose that's not a bad idea for inspiration on how religious extremists can operate, though I guess I'm really looking for an interesting doctrinal incompatibility to use as inspiration for Cartwright's faction.<br /> <br /> I went into the Dark Eras draft from the Kickstarter, and there's an idea percolating. One thing heavily frowned upon by the Sanctified is the implication that vampires will gain some kind of salvation. Promising a heavenly reward to creatures who eternally walk the earth seems pretty paradoxical, but what if the Reverend preaches a creed which implies there's some light at the end of the tunnel? That's a really basic idea that lacks the nuance of specifics to nail it down, but I could definitely see it appealing to troubled young vampires. I think I might chew on that for a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}